## Why This Is Asked
This question tests mastery of maintaining order statistics with dynamic updates, handling duplicates efficiently, and implementing lazy deletion—all while achieving O(log n) time complexity.

## Key Concepts
- **Two heaps for median maintenance**: A max-heap stores the lower half, while a min-heap stores the upper half, allowing O(1) median retrieval
- **Duplicate handling**: Store actual values in heaps with a frequency counter map to track occurrences
- **Lazy deletion**: Defer removals by updating a delayed-delete map; prune elements lazily when they surface at heap tops to achieve O(log n) amortized erase

## Code Example
```python
import heapq

class DualHeap:
    def __init__(self):
        self.small = []  # max-heap (store negatives)
        self.large = []  # min-heap
        self.delayed = {}  # lazy deletion map
        self.small_size = 0
        self.large_size = 0

    def prune(self, heap):
        while heap:
            num = -heap[0] if heap is self.small else heap[0]
            if self.delayed.get(num, 0) > 0:
                heapq.heappop(heap)
                self.delayed[num] -= 1
                if self.delayed[num] == 0:
                    del self.delayed[num]
            else:
                break

    def rebalance(self):
        if self.small_size > self.large_size + 1:
            val = -heapq.heappop(self.small)
            self.small_size -= 1
            heapq.heappush(self.large, val)
            self.large_size += 1
        elif self.large_size > self.small_size + 1:
            val = heapq.heappop(self.large)
            self.large_size -= 1
            heapq.heappush(self.small, -val)
            self.small_size += 1

    def insert(self, num):
        if not self.small or num <= -self.small[0]:
            heapq.heappush(self.small, -num)
            self.small_size += 1
        else:
            heapq.heappush(self.large, num)
            self.large_size += 1
        self.rebalance()

    def erase(self, num):
        self.delayed[num] = self.delayed.get(num, 0) + 1
        if num <= -self.small[0]:
            self.small_size -= 1
        else:
            self.large_size -= 1
        self.rebalance()

    def getMedian(self):
        if self.small_size > self.large_size:
            self.prune(self.small)
            return -self.small[0]
        elif self.large_size > self.small_size:
            self.prune(self.large)
            return self.large[0]
        return (-self.small[0] + self.large[0]) / 2
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of maintaining an ordered dynamic sequence with logarithmic updates while augmenting nodes with aggregate data for fast queries.

## Key Concepts
- Implicit treap for sequence indexing
- Split by position and merge operations
- Augmented data: size and sum to support rangeSum
- Handling duplicates via node values and randomized priorities

## Code Example
```javascript
class Node { constructor(val){ this.val=val; this.pri=Math.random(); this.left=null; this.right=null; this.sz=1; this.sum=val; } }
function sz(n){ return n? n.sz:0; }
function sum(n){ return n? n.sum:0; }
function upd(n){ if(n){ n.sz = 1 + sz(n.left) + sz(n.right); n.sum = n.val + sum(n.left) + sum(n.right); } }
function split(root, key){ // first key elements go to left
  if(!root) return [null,null];
  if(sz(root.left) >= key){ const [l,r] = split(root.left, key); root.left = r; upd(root); return [l, root]; }
  else { const [l,r] = split(root.right, key - sz(root.left) - 1); root.right = l; upd(root); return [root, r]; }
}
function merge(a,b){ if(!a||!b) return a||b; if(a.pri < b.pri){ a.right = merge(a.right, b); upd(a); return a; } else { b.left = merge(a, b.left); upd(b); return b; } }
function insertAt(root, index, value){ const node = new Node(value); const [L,R] = split(root, index); return merge(merge(L, node), R); }
function eraseAt(root, index){ const [L, R] = split(root, index); const [M, RR] = split(R, 1); return merge(L, RR); }
function rangeSumQuery(root, l, r){ const [A, BR] = split(root, l); const [B, C] = split(BR, r - l + 1); const res = sum(B); const newRoot = merge(A, merge(B, C)); return {root: newRoot, sum: res}; }
```

